@startuml
title Monthly report generation (scheduled) + BO view

participant "Worker (Procrastinate)" as Worker
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB
actor Staff
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js BO)" as FE

== Scheduled generation (1st of each month) ==
Worker -> BE : periodic reports.generate_previous_month_reports
note over Worker
  Cron "0 2 1 * *" (UTC). Task body has no business logic —
  delegates to the service layer (background-jobs.md).
end note
BE -> BE : for each staff: reports.services.generate_monthly_report(prev month)
BE -> BE : analytics.selectors.compute_staff_monthly_metrics()
note over BE
  Reads appointments via the appointments selector layer (anti-corruption).
  Metrics: hours worked, appts booked/made/canceled/no-show,
  distinct + new clients, top-3 services, revenue (total & per service),
  revenue per hour. Revenue uses the booking-time price snapshot (ADR 0001);
  quote-only appointments contribute no revenue.
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT appointments (local month range)
BE -> DB : UPSERT reports_monthly_report (unique staff+year+month)

== View in BO ==
Staff -> FE : open Reports
FE -> NGINX : GET /bo/v1/reports/  (Cookie: sessionid)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  AuthN: session; AuthZ: IsStaffMember
  staff see only their own reports; admin may pass ?staff_id
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT reports_monthly_report
BE --> FE : 200 (MonthlyReportSerializer[])
FE --> Staff : monthly metrics

note over Staff, DB
  Staff/admin can also trigger generation on demand:
  POST /bo/v1/reports/generate { year, month, staff_id? }
end note
@enduml
